    ('q-pr89-rfib-01-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Seagrass Recovery: Restoration Hurdles', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Efforts to repair damaged seagrass habitats require innovative planting methodologies. Technicians frequently broadcast seeds or manually [[b1]] nursery-grown shoots into bare substrates. However, vigorous tidal currents often [[b2]] unrooted seedlings before their underground rhizomes can establish a firm [[b3]] in the seabed.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "transplant"}, {"id": "B", "text": "dislodge"}, {"id": "C", "text": "foothold"}, {"id": "D", "text": "abandon"}, {"id": "E", "text": "nourish"}, {"id": "F", "text": "barrier"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["transplant", "dislodge", "foothold", "abandon", "nourish", "barrier"], "correctAnswer": "transplant"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["transplant", "dislodge", "foothold", "abandon", "nourish", "barrier"], "correctAnswer": "dislodge"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["transplant", "dislodge", "foothold", "abandon", "nourish", "barrier"], "correctAnswer": "foothold"}]'::jsonb,
     'Technicians transplant shoots (replant), currents dislodge seedlings (uproot), before establishing a foothold (secure grip).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-001', 'g-pr89-001-rfib', 5, TRUE, 120, NULL),
