     'Seagrass Climatology: Blue Carbon Burial', 'According to paragraph D, what enables seagrass sediment to store carbon for centuries without decomposing?',
     NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "The continuous freezing temperatures of shallow coastal waters halt chemical reactions"}, {"id": "B", "text": "The permanently waterlogged, saline, and anoxic environment suppresses microbial decomposition"}, {"id": "C", "text": "The high concentrations of toxic heavy metals prevent bacteria from surviving"}, {"id": "D", "text": "The periodic burning of dried surface blades turns carbon into inert charcoal"}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
     'Paragraph D states that in a permanently submerged, saline, and completely anoxic setting, microbial decomposition proceeds at a negligible rate.', 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-001', 'g-pr89-001-single', 4, TRUE, 90, NULL),
