    ('q-pr89-rwfib-02-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Subsea Infrastructure: Optical Transmission', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'While many assume satellites carry the majority of international traffic, modern data networks depend on underwater cables. Over ninety-five percent of all transoceanic communications [[b1]] through submarine fiber-optic conduits resting on the ocean floor. By utilizing dense wavelength division multiplexing, a single contemporary cable can [[b2]] hundreds of terabits per second. This remarkable capacity has made submarine lines the [[b3]] foundation of global digital commerce.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["falter", "flow", "stagnate", "stray"], "correctAnswer": "flow"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["dissipate", "suppress", "transmit", "withhold"], "correctAnswer": "transmit"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["indispensable", "precarious", "provisional", "superfluous"], "correctAnswer": "indispensable"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''flow'' denotes continuous data transit (''stray'' means wander off; ''falter'' means hesitate/weaken; ''stagnate'' means cease moving). b2: ''transmit'' means sending signals (''withhold'', ''suppress'', and ''dissipate'' mean holding back or wasting energy). b3: ''indispensable'' matches supporting 95% of traffic (''superfluous'' means unneeded; ''provisional'' means temporary; ''precarious'' means dangerously unstable).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-02-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Subsea Architecture: Core Composition', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The interior design of a deep-water cable balances optical protection with electrical power delivery. At the center are delicate glass fibers surrounded by petroleum jelly, which [[b1]] moisture penetration. Encasing these fibers is a conductive metallic tube that [[b2]] high-voltage direct current to submerged optical repeaters. In the undisturbed plains of the deep abyss, cables require little external armor and [[b3]] in diameter to common household hoses.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["absorbs", "hastens", "inhibits", "invites"], "correctAnswer": "inhibits"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["consumes", "intercepts", "supplies", "withholds"], "correctAnswer": "supplies"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["alternate", "approximate", "deviate", "dissent"], "correctAnswer": "approximate"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''inhibits'' means prevents water ingress (''hastens'' and ''invites'' mean increasing penetration; ''absorbs'' contradicts water-repellent jelly). b2: ''supplies'' means powering repeaters (''consumes'' means using power; ''intercepts'' means blocking; ''withholds'' means refusing to give). b3: ''approximate to'' is the correct construction for similarity in size (''dissent from'', ''deviate from'', and ''alternate with'' take different prepositions and meanings).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-02-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Subsea Installation: Shelf Burial', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'In shallow coastal waters, undersea cables face constant hazards from commercial maritime activity. To protect lines from heavy anchors and fishing nets, ships [[b1]] armored cables deep within marine sediments. A towed submersible plow cuts a trench into the seabed, [[b2]] the cable several metres below the surface. Over subsequent weeks, shifting sea currents [[b3]] silt over the trench, insulating the installation from mechanical impact.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["abandon", "discard", "embed", "suspend"], "correctAnswer": "embed"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["depositing", "extracting", "retrieving", "withdrawing"], "correctAnswer": "depositing"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["accumulate", "disperse", "drain", "erode"], "correctAnswer": "accumulate"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''embed'' means placing firmly into the seabed (''discard'' and ''abandon'' mean throwing away; ''suspend'' means hanging in water). b2: ''depositing'' means laying down (''extracting'', ''withdrawing'', and ''retrieving'' mean pulling out of the ground). b3: ''accumulate'' describes sediment building up (''disperse'', ''erode'', and ''drain'' mean removing material).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-02-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Subsea Maintenance: Fault Detection', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'When an underwater cable suffers a rupture, finding the break requires sophisticated diagnostic techniques. Engineers at landing stations transmit brief laser pulses along the fiber and [[b1]] the reflected optical signals. By measuring the precise time delay of the reflection, they can [[b2]] the location of the severance within metres. A specialized vessel is then [[b3]] to initiate maritime repair procedures.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["analyze", "distort", "misread", "scramble"], "correctAnswer": "analyze"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["approximate", "misjudge", "overestimate", "pinpoint"], "correctAnswer": "pinpoint"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["decommissioned", "dispatched", "diverted", "quarantined"], "correctAnswer": "dispatched"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''analyze'' means evaluating diagnostic data (''distort'', ''scramble'', and ''misread'' describe corrupting signals). b2: ''pinpoint'' means locating with exact precision (''approximate'' means guessing roughly; ''misjudge'' and ''overestimate'' mean calculating incorrectly). b3: ''dispatched'' means deployed to the scene (''decommissioned'' means retired; ''quarantined'' means isolated; ''diverted'' means sent away).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-02-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Subsea Topography: Choke Point Risks', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Global connectivity depends heavily on narrow maritime corridors where numerous cables converge. Natural tremors or anchoring incidents in these congested zones can [[b1]] multiple lines simultaneously. To prevent catastrophic blackouts, international networks are [[b2]] alternative routing corridors. Establishing diverse geographical pathways [[b3]] systemic vulnerability across the international data grid.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["insulate", "reconnect", "reinforce", "sever"], "correctAnswer": "sever"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["abandoning", "banning", "evading", "pioneering"], "correctAnswer": "pioneering"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["aggravates", "induces", "mitigates", "multiplies"], "correctAnswer": "mitigates"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''sever'' means cutting lines (''insulate'', ''reconnect'', and ''reinforce'' describe protecting or joining). b2: ''pioneering'' means developing new paths (''abandoning'' means giving up; ''banning'' means outlawing; ''evading'' means dodging). b3: ''mitigates'' means reducing vulnerability (''aggravates'', ''multiplies'', and ''induces'' mean increasing risks).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-02-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Subsea Cable Anatomy: Signal Repeaters', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Optical data signals traveling through hundreds of kilometres of glass fiber inevitably experience attenuation. To maintain transmission strength, engineers install optical [[b1]] at regular intervals along the seafloor. These devices receive electrical power through an internal copper conductor that carries high-voltage [[b2]] current from coastal terminal facilities, ensuring optical pulses retain sufficient [[b3]] to cross entire oceans.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "repeaters"}, {"id": "B", "text": "direct"}, {"id": "C", "text": "intensity"}, {"id": "D", "text": "amplifiers"}, {"id": "E", "text": "continuous"}, {"id": "F", "text": "frequency"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["repeaters", "direct", "intensity", "amplifiers", "continuous", "frequency"], "correctAnswer": "repeaters"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["repeaters", "direct", "intensity", "amplifiers", "continuous", "frequency"], "correctAnswer": "direct"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["repeaters", "direct", "intensity", "amplifiers", "continuous", "frequency"], "correctAnswer": "intensity"}]'::jsonb,
     'Engineers install optical repeaters (signal boosters), powered by direct current (DC electrical power), ensuring signal intensity (strength).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rfib', 1, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-02-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Subsea Cable Deployment: Seabed Silt', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Laying an armored cable across shallow coastal shelves requires careful bathymetric navigation. Cable ships tow a massive submersible plow that slices through bottom [[b1]] to deposit the line in a protective furrow. Once installed, natural sedimentary movement gradually covers the trench, creating a protective [[b2]] against dragging anchors and commercial fishing [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "sediments"}, {"id": "B", "text": "barrier"}, {"id": "C", "text": "gear"}, {"id": "D", "text": "bedrock"}, {"id": "E", "text": "shield"}, {"id": "F", "text": "anchors"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["sediments", "barrier", "gear", "bedrock", "shield", "anchors"], "correctAnswer": "sediments"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["sediments", "barrier", "gear", "bedrock", "shield", "anchors"], "correctAnswer": "barrier"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["sediments", "barrier", "gear", "bedrock", "shield", "anchors"], "correctAnswer": "gear"}]'::jsonb,
     'The plow slices sediments (seabed mud/sand), creating a protective barrier (shield), guarding against fishing gear (trawl equipment).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-002', 'g-pr89-002-rfib', 2, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-02-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Subsea Hazards: Geologic Tremors', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Seismic activity on the ocean floor presents a major physical hazard to subsea communications. When an undersea earthquake occurs, it can trigger massive [[b1]] avalanches that tear down continental slopes. These violent mudflows travel at high speed and can easily [[b2]] heavily armored cables, causing widespread telecommunication [[b3]] across entire geographic regions.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "turbidity"}, {"id": "B", "text": "rupture"}, {"id": "C", "text": "outages"}, {"id": "D", "text": "density"}, {"id": "E", "text": "fracture"}, {"id": "F", "text": "interruptions"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["turbidity", "rupture", "outages", "density", "fracture", "interruptions"], "correctAnswer": "turbidity"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["turbidity", "rupture", "outages", "density", "fracture", "interruptions"], "correctAnswer": "rupture"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["turbidity", "rupture", "outages", "density", "fracture", "interruptions"], "correctAnswer": "outages"}]'::jsonb,
