    ('q-pr89-rwfib-03-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Dromedary Domestication: Archaeological Sequence', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'For centuries, the precise chronology of camel domestication remained uncertain. Recent archaeological excavations in southeast Arabia have finally [[b1]] this historical timeline. Before the late second millennium BCE, wild dromedaries were hunted as game animals rather than [[b2]] as working pack animals. Once tamed, the species expanded across arid regions with remarkable [[b3]], transforming desert mobility.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["clarified", "delayed", "fabricated", "obscured"], "correctAnswer": "clarified"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["abandoned", "demolished", "evacuated", "maintained"], "correctAnswer": "maintained"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["fragility", "hesitation", "reluctance", "speed"], "correctAnswer": "speed"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''clarified'' means resolving uncertainty (''obscured'' means making unclear; ''delayed'' means postponing; ''fabricated'' means forging evidence). b2: ''maintained'' means keeping and caring for working stock (''abandoned'' means left behind; ''demolished'' applies to structures; ''evacuated'' means clearing people). b3: ''speed'' matches rapid expansion (''hesitation'', ''fragility'', and ''reluctance'' denote slow or fragile progress).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
