     'Faunal Demographics: Herd Mortality Profiles', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Zooarchaeologists identify camel domestication by analyzing bone assemblages from excavated settlements. Domestic layers exhibit distinct mortality profiles where female camels were [[b1]] into old age for breeding and milk production. Concurrently, younger male camels were routinely [[b2]] to provide meat. Chemical analysis of pottery sherds has confirmed that camel dairying had become a major economic [[b3]] of early oasis life.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["condemned", "culled", "neglected", "preserved"], "correctAnswer": "preserved"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["cultivated", "harvested", "promoted", "rewarded"], "correctAnswer": "harvested"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["deterrent", "hazard", "penalty", "pillar"], "correctAnswer": "pillar"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''preserved'' means kept alive for dairying (''culled'' means slaughtered; ''condemned'' and ''neglected'' mean mistreated). b2: ''harvested'' is standard agricultural terminology for processing meat animals (''promoted'' and ''rewarded'' apply to people; ''cultivated'' applies to crops). b3: ''pillar'' denotes a central foundation (''deterrent'', ''hazard'', and ''penalty'' denote obstacles or punishments).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-03-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Physiological Endurance: Water Conservation', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The survival of the dromedary in extreme arid climates depends on specialized evolutionary adaptations. Specialized nasal passages condense exhaled moisture and [[b1]] water loss to the dry desert air. Furthermore, concentration of body fat inside the dorsal hump prevents heat from being [[b2]] within the animal''s muscle tissue. Broad, cushioned footpads allow camels to navigate shifting sand dunes without [[b3]] into loose terrain.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["accelerate", "amplify", "diminish", "magnify"], "correctAnswer": "diminish"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["expelled", "purified", "radiated", "trapped"], "correctAnswer": "trapped"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["drifting", "gliding", "sinking", "soaring"], "correctAnswer": "sinking"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''diminish'' means reducing moisture loss (''amplify'', ''accelerate'', and ''magnify'' mean increasing loss). b2: ''trapped'' means retained internally (''radiated'' and ''expelled'' mean emitted outward; ''purified'' means cleansed). b3: ''sinking'' describes foot penetration into sand (''soaring'' means flying high; ''drifting'' and ''gliding'' imply smooth effortless movement).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-03-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Pack Saddle Technology: Load Distribution', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Early camel riders sat behind the hump, but transport efficiency remained limited until the invention of the rigid pack saddle. The South Arabian saddle utilized a wooden frame that [[b1]] heavy freight loads across the animal''s ribcage. This innovative design protected the sensitive spine from [[b2]] while securing cargo bundles firmly. With this equipment, caravans could transport valuable merchandise across deserts without [[b3]] the animals.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["accumulated", "concentrated", "distributed", "isolated"], "correctAnswer": "distributed"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["elevation", "injury", "nutrition", "stagnation"], "correctAnswer": "injury"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["harming", "insulating", "nourishing", "protecting"], "correctAnswer": "harming"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''distributed'' means spreading weight across ribs (''concentrated'', ''accumulated'', and ''isolated'' mean focusing on one spot, which injures the spine). b2: ''injury'' denotes physical harm (''nutrition'', ''stagnation'', and ''elevation'' are contextually absurd). b3: ''harming'' fits the negative clause ''without harming'' (''nourishing'', ''protecting'', and ''insulating'' mean helping).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
