     'Caravan Economics: Overland Incense Corridors', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The emergence of regular camel caravans opened lucrative trans-Arabian trade corridors. Merchant caravans transported frankincense and myrrh from southern harvesting regions across the desert [[b1]] to Mediterranean harbors. The high value of these aromatic resins [[b2]] the establishment of fortified oasis towns along the route. Over time, these transit networks [[b3]] isolated desert tribes with major international markets.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["estuaries", "interior", "suburbs", "wetlands"], "correctAnswer": "interior"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["discouraged", "prohibited", "stimulated", "suppressed"], "correctAnswer": "stimulated"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["connected", "isolated", "segregated", "threatened"], "correctAnswer": "connected"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''interior'' denotes the inland desert heartland (''suburbs'', ''estuaries'', and ''wetlands'' describe urban or coastal aquatic environments). b2: ''stimulated'' means spurred economic growth (''discouraged'', ''prohibited'', and ''suppressed'' mean hindering). b3: ''connected'' denotes linking communities (''isolated'', ''segregated'', and ''threatened'' mean separating or endangering).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
