     'Arid Pastoralism: Camel Domestication Origins', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Archaeological surveys in the southern Arabian Peninsula have clarified the emergence of camel husbandry. Before regular domestication, local foragers hunted wild herds for meat and raw [[b1]]. Following the drying of regional grasslands, pastoralists shifted toward active captive [[b2]] and selective breeding, establishing a resilient working relationship with desert [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "materials"}, {"id": "B", "text": "management"}, {"id": "C", "text": "communities"}, {"id": "D", "text": "substances"}, {"id": "E", "text": "governance"}, {"id": "F", "text": "settlements"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["materials", "management", "communities", "substances", "governance", "settlements"], "correctAnswer": "materials"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["materials", "management", "communities", "substances", "governance", "settlements"], "correctAnswer": "management"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["materials", "management", "communities", "substances", "governance", "settlements"], "correctAnswer": "communities"}]'::jsonb,
