     'Skeletal Differentiation: Bone Proportions', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Zooarchaeologists distinguish wild and domestic camel remains by measuring bone dimensions. Domestic dromedaries exhibit more gracile skeletal structures than their larger wild [[b1]]. In addition, excavation layers containing domestic stock show high numbers of mature female [[b2]], confirming that herds were conserved primarily for regular milk [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "ancestors"}, {"id": "B", "text": "animals"}, {"id": "C", "text": "yields"}, {"id": "D", "text": "predecessors"}, {"id": "E", "text": "specimens"}, {"id": "F", "text": "harvests"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["ancestors", "animals", "yields", "predecessors", "specimens", "harvests"], "correctAnswer": "ancestors"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["ancestors", "animals", "yields", "predecessors", "specimens", "harvests"], "correctAnswer": "animals"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["ancestors", "animals", "yields", "predecessors", "specimens", "harvests"], "correctAnswer": "yields"}]'::jsonb,
