     'Thermal Regulation: Cellular Adaptations', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The dromedary possesses notable physiological mechanisms for conserving moisture during extreme heat. When dehydrated camels drink, their oval red blood cells absorb water and expand without experiencing [[b1]]. Meanwhile, concentrating body fat inside the dorsal hump prevents heat from building up across muscular [[b2]], allowing the animal to maintain a stable internal [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "rupture"}, {"id": "B", "text": "tissue"}, {"id": "C", "text": "temperature"}, {"id": "D", "text": "fracture"}, {"id": "E", "text": "fiber"}, {"id": "F", "text": "circulation"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["rupture", "tissue", "temperature", "fracture", "fiber", "circulation"], "correctAnswer": "rupture"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["rupture", "tissue", "temperature", "fracture", "fiber", "circulation"], "correctAnswer": "tissue"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["rupture", "tissue", "temperature", "fracture", "fiber", "circulation"], "correctAnswer": "temperature"}]'::jsonb,
