    ('q-pr89-rfib-03-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Saddle Engineering: Spinal Protection', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Carrying heavy commercial cargo across long desert distances required specialized equipment. The South Arabian pack saddle utilized a wooden frame designed to rest upon the animal''s strong [[b1]]. By elevating freight bundles away from the dorsal ridge, the saddle prevented painful pressure on delicate [[b2]], enabling pack animals to transport heavy goods over demanding [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "ribs"}, {"id": "B", "text": "vertebrae"}, {"id": "C", "text": "routes"}, {"id": "D", "text": "shoulders"}, {"id": "E", "text": "bones"}, {"id": "F", "text": "trails"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["ribs", "vertebrae", "routes", "shoulders", "bones", "trails"], "correctAnswer": "ribs"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["ribs", "vertebrae", "routes", "shoulders", "bones", "trails"], "correctAnswer": "vertebrae"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["ribs", "vertebrae", "routes", "shoulders", "bones", "trails"], "correctAnswer": "routes"}]'::jsonb,
     'Weight rested on the animal ribs (torso frame), avoiding pressure on vertebrae (spine), traveling over demanding routes (paths).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rfib', 4, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-03-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Genetic Heritage: Wild Interbreeding', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Unlike other domestic livestock that suffered severe genetic bottlenecks, domestic dromedaries retained substantial biological diversity. For centuries, pastoralists allowed domestic herds to breed with surviving wild [[b1]]. This ongoing genetic exchange introduced valuable immune [[b2]] and helped preserve the health and adaptability of modern camel [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "populations"}, {"id": "B", "text": "traits"}, {"id": "C", "text": "lineages"}, {"id": "D", "text": "colonies"}, {"id": "E", "text": "features"}, {"id": "F", "text": "breeds"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["populations", "traits", "lineages", "colonies", "features", "breeds"], "correctAnswer": "populations"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["populations", "traits", "lineages", "colonies", "features", "breeds"], "correctAnswer": "traits"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["populations", "traits", "lineages", "colonies", "features", "breeds"], "correctAnswer": "lineages"}]'::jsonb,
     'Herds mated with wild populations (groups), introducing immune traits (characteristics), preserving domestic lineages (bloodlines).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-003', 'g-pr89-003-rfib', 5, TRUE, 120, NULL),
