    ('q-pr89-rwfib-04-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Ancient Harbours: Natural Shelters', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Early Mediterranean societies depended heavily on coastal geography for maritime security. Before the invention of hydraulic mortar, navigators sought natural anchorages in sheltered bays or leeward islands where galleys were [[b1]] from destructive offshore gales. At early Phoenician and Greek ports, human modification was largely [[b2]] to constructing rudimentary stone barriers along the shore. However, these natural havens were geographically scarce and could not [[b3]] the growing volume of bulk trade demanded by imperial populations.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["barred", "deterred", "exempted", "shielded"], "correctAnswer": "shielded"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["allotted", "attuned", "confined", "subjected"], "correctAnswer": "confined"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["accommodate", "disembark", "evacuate", "navigate"], "correctAnswer": "accommodate"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''shielded from'' is the correct physical protection construction (''exempted from'' applies to legal taxes; ''deterred from'' applies to human choices; ''barred from'' applies to entering spaces). b2: ''confined to'' denotes geographic limitation (''subjected to'' means suffering; ''allotted to'' means distributing; ''attuned to'' means adjusting mentally). b3: ''accommodate'' means harboring ships (''disembark'' applies to passengers; ''evacuate'' means emptying; ''navigate'' is an active steering action done by captains, not coves).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-04-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Pozzolanic Concrete: Submarine Mortar', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Roman builders achieved a breakthrough in civil engineering with the perfection of hydraulic concrete. By blending volcanic ash from Pozzuoli with slaked lime and seawater, they created a material capable of [[b1]] underwater. Modern analyses demonstrate that chemical reactions within the concrete precipitate interlocking crystals that [[b2]] the structure over centuries. Consequently, Roman maritime breakwaters remained [[b3]] despite millennia of wave impact.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["decaying", "dissolving", "fracturing", "hardening"], "correctAnswer": "hardening"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["corrode", "destabilize", "strengthen", "weaken"], "correctAnswer": "strengthen"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["dormant", "frail", "intact", "obsolete"], "correctAnswer": "intact"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''hardening'' describes concrete setting underwater (''dissolving'', ''decaying'', and ''fracturing'' mean disintegrating). b2: ''strengthen'' describes mineral crystallization reinforcing the matrix (''corrode'', ''weaken'', and ''destabilize'' mean degrading). b3: ''intact'' means physically undamaged (''frail'' means weak; ''dormant'' means sleeping; ''obsolete'' means out of date).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-04-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Portus Basin: Caisson Construction', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The construction of the imperial harbour at Portus showcased Roman engineering mastery. To build breakwaters far into open water, engineers constructed massive wooden caissons that were [[b1]] into position by tugboats. Once aligned, workers packed the wooden frames with pozzolanic concrete until the structures [[b2]] to the seabed. This technique enabled the creation of monumental basins that offered [[b3]] shelter to hundreds of merchant vessels.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["diverted", "flung", "stranded", "towed"], "correctAnswer": "towed"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["ascended", "drifted", "rebounded", "sank"], "correctAnswer": "sank"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["dependable", "fleeting", "hazardous", "negligible"], "correctAnswer": "dependable"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''towed'' describes tugboats pulling heavy caissons (''flung'' implies throwing; ''stranded'' means stuck; ''diverted'' means turned away). b2: ''sank'' means descending to the seabed (''drifted'' means floating away; ''ascended'' means rising; ''rebounded'' means bouncing). b3: ''dependable'' matches reliable shelter (''hazardous'' means unsafe; ''fleeting'' means brief; ''negligible'' means tiny).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-04-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Harbour Siltation: Alluvial Infilling', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Despite structural durability, ancient harbours faced a persistent threat from alluvial sediment. When river currents entered quiet harbour basins, water velocities dropped, causing suspended particles to [[b1]] onto the basin floor. Widespread deforestation and hillside agriculture upstream dramatically [[b2]] soil erosion rates. Over centuries, continuous siltation [[b3]] active commercial ports into landlocked marshes.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["rebound", "scatter", "settle", "soar"], "correctAnswer": "settle"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["accelerated", "curbed", "moderated", "suppressed"], "correctAnswer": "accelerated"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["exempted", "preserved", "restored", "transformed"], "correctAnswer": "transformed"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''settle'' means depositing on the floor (''scatter'' means spreading; ''rebound'' means bouncing; ''soar'' means flying upward). b2: ''accelerated'' matches tenfold erosion increases (''moderated'', ''curbed'', and ''suppressed'' mean decreasing). b3: ''transformed'' describes changing ports into marshes (''restored'' and ''preserved'' mean keeping clean; ''exempted'' means freed from duty).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-04-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Harbour Scouring: Arched Moles', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'To keep shipping channels open, Roman hydraulic architects implemented innovative design elements. They constructed breakwaters supported on pillars with open arches that allowed coastal currents to [[b1]] through the basin. This continuous water movement helped [[b2]] away loose sand before it could form permanent sandbars. When passive currents proved inadequate, port authorities deployed mechanical dredging machines to [[b3]] the channel.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["cease", "flow", "recoil", "stagnate"], "correctAnswer": "flow"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["cement", "compress", "deposit", "scour"], "correctAnswer": "scour"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["constrict", "deepen", "obstruct", "shallow"], "correctAnswer": "deepen"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''flow'' describes current movement through arches (''cease'' and ''stagnate'' mean stopping; ''recoil'' means flinching). b2: ''scour away'' means washing sand out (''compress'', ''deposit'', and ''cement'' mean compacting or adding sand). b3: ''deepen'' describes clearing navigational draft (''obstruct'' and ''constrict'' mean narrowing or blocking; ''shallow'' as a verb is non-standard or opposite).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-04-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Roman Concrete: Chemical Reaction', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The durability of Roman marine structures stems from unique geochemical properties. When pozzolanic ash reacts with lime and seawater, it forms specialized mineral [[b1]] that fill microscopic fissures. This continuous crystallization prevents seawater from causing internal structural [[b2]], allowing ancient breakwaters to retain their [[b3]] over millennia.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "crystals"}, {"id": "B", "text": "fractures"}, {"id": "C", "text": "integrity"}, {"id": "D", "text": "minerals"}, {"id": "E", "text": "cavities"}, {"id": "F", "text": "durability"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["crystals", "fractures", "integrity", "minerals", "cavities", "durability"], "correctAnswer": "crystals"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["crystals", "fractures", "integrity", "minerals", "cavities", "durability"], "correctAnswer": "fractures"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["crystals", "fractures", "integrity", "minerals", "cavities", "durability"], "correctAnswer": "integrity"}]'::jsonb,
     'Reaction forms mineral crystals (crystallized structures), preventing internal fractures (cracks), maintaining integrity (wholeness).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rfib', 1, TRUE, 120, NULL),
