    ('q-pr89-rfib-04-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Flushing Systems: Sluice Mechanisms', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'To clear accumulating sediment from berths, Roman architects devised dynamic flushing mechanisms. Enclosed holding reservoirs collected water at high tide behind heavy wooden [[b1]]. During low tide, operators opened the gates, releasing a violent pulse of water that flushed settled mud out through the harbour [[b2]], preserving the required navigational [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "gates"}, {"id": "B", "text": "mouth"}, {"id": "C", "text": "depth"}, {"id": "D", "text": "barriers"}, {"id": "E", "text": "entrance"}, {"id": "F", "text": "clearance"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["gates", "mouth", "depth", "barriers", "entrance", "clearance"], "correctAnswer": "gates"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["gates", "mouth", "depth", "barriers", "entrance", "clearance"], "correctAnswer": "mouth"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["gates", "mouth", "depth", "barriers", "entrance", "clearance"], "correctAnswer": "depth"}]'::jsonb,
     'Reservoirs stored water behind gates (sluices), flushing sediment out the mouth (entrance), maintaining navigation depth (clearance).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-004', 'g-pr89-004-rfib', 4, TRUE, 120, NULL),
