    ('q-pr89-rwfib-05-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Lava Tube Formation: Thermal Insulation', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Basaltic lava tubes develop during effusive eruptions of fluid lava. As molten pahoehoe streams down a volcanic flank, the outer layer chills upon contact with the air and [[b1]] into a solid basalt crust. This rock roof acts as an extraordinary thermal insulator that [[b2]] heat loss to barely one degree Celsius per kilometre. Beneath this protective shell, molten lava continues flowing freely until the vent ceases effusion and the internal fluid [[b3]] downslope.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["evaporates", "liquefies", "pulverizes", "solidifies"], "correctAnswer": "solidifies"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["facilitates", "invites", "promotes", "restricts"], "correctAnswer": "restricts"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["accumulates", "drains", "overflows", "stagnates"], "correctAnswer": "drains"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''solidifies'' describes crust hardening (''evaporates'' applies to liquids; ''liquefies'' means melting; ''pulverizes'' means grinding to powder). b2: ''restricts'' describes insulating crust slowing heat loss (''facilitates'', ''promotes'', and ''invites'' mean encouraging loss). b3: ''drains'' describes molten lava emptying out (''accumulates'', ''overflows'', and ''stagnates'' mean staying or filling).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-05-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Volcanic Speleothems: Conduit Features', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'When the molten lava drains from a subterranean tunnel, it leaves behind distinctive structural features. Successive drops in the fluid level produce horizontal [[b1]] along the walls that indicate previous high-water marks. From the ceiling vaults, dripping molten stone forms slender volcanic stalactites known as lavacicles. In some high-volume conduits, the hot stream can [[b2]] deep trenches into the underlying bedrock, producing complex [[b3]] passages.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["crevasses", "ledges", "potholes", "trenches"], "correctAnswer": "ledges"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["carve", "fill", "patch", "smooth"], "correctAnswer": "carve"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["flat", "hollow", "multi-level", "straight"], "correctAnswer": "multi-level"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''ledges'' describes horizontal mineral shelves left by declining flow (''crevasses'', ''trenches'', and ''potholes'' are depressions or cracks). b2: ''carve'' describes thermal erosion cutting down into rock (''fill'', ''patch'', and ''smooth'' describe leveling or adding material). b3: ''multi-level'' matches stacked galleries formed by subsequent eruptions (''flat'', ''hollow'', and ''straight'' are irrelevant geometry).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-05-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Volcanic Skylights: Microclimate Oases', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Over centuries, seismic tremors and weathering cause sections of thin basalt roofs to collapse. These vertical openings, known as skylights, [[b1]] ambient sunlight and moisture into dark galleries. Enclosed within protective basalt walls, relative humidity remains [[b2]] while shielding vegetation from exterior winds. Consequently, lush communities of ferns and mosses can [[b3]] directly on fallen boulder cones.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["exclude", "extinguish", "introduce", "suppress"], "correctAnswer": "introduce"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["consistently", "erratically", "scarcely", "sporadically"], "correctAnswer": "consistently"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["dwindle", "flourish", "perish", "wither"], "correctAnswer": "flourish"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''introduce'' describes roof skylights admitting daylight (''exclude'', ''extinguish'', and ''suppress'' mean keeping light out). b2: ''consistently'' describes stable subterranean microclimates (''erratically'', ''scarcely'', and ''sporadically'' mean unstable or rare). b3: ''flourish'' describes specialized ferns thriving (''perish'', ''dwindle'', and ''wither'' mean dying).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-05-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Troglobitic Biology: Cave Adaptations', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Deep inside lava tubes, permanent darkness fosters the evolution of obligate cave animals. Troglobites exhibit specialized physical adaptations, such as the complete [[b1]] of body pigment and functional eyes. To navigate their subterranean environment, these creatures rely on [[b2]] sensory antennae and heightened tactile sensitivity. Because food resources are scarce, they have also evolved [[b3]] metabolic rates.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["absence", "abundance", "diffusion", "excess"], "correctAnswer": "absence"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["constricted", "elongated", "shrunken", "stunted"], "correctAnswer": "elongated"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["accelerated", "depressed", "elevated", "inflated"], "correctAnswer": "depressed"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''absence of'' denotes lacking pigment (''excess'' and ''abundance'' mean having too much; ''diffusion'' means spreading). b2: ''elongated'' describes lengthened antennae for sensory compensation (''stunted'', ''constricted'', and ''shrunken'' mean shortened). b3: ''depressed'' describes reduced metabolic rates to conserve energy in scarce food regimes (''inflated'', ''elevated'', and ''accelerated'' mean increased).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-05-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Lava Tube Astrobiology: Planetary Analogue', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Planetary scientists study basaltic tubes as potential habitats for future space exploration. Orbital satellites have detected enormous lava conduits on both the Moon and Mars that [[b1]] hundreds of metres in width. On Mars, thick basalt ceilings could [[b2]] human outposts from deadly cosmic radiation and micrometeorites. Understanding terrestrial tube ecosystems thus provides critical [[b3]] for interplanetary science.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["disregard", "fabricate", "measure", "overlook"], "correctAnswer": "measure"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["abandon", "relegate", "shield", "subject"], "correctAnswer": "shield"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["hindrances", "illusions", "insights", "setbacks"], "correctAnswer": "insights"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''measure'' describes surveying cave geometry (''fabricate'' means making up; ''disregard'' and ''overlook'' mean ignoring). b2: ''shield ... from'' is the correct protective construction (''subject'', ''abandon'', and ''relegate'' take ''to'' and imply vulnerability). b3: ''insights'' denotes valuable scientific understanding (''hindrances'', ''setbacks'', and ''illusions'' denote obstacles or errors).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-05-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Lava Tube Formation: Pahoehoe Flow', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Basaltic conduits require specific thermal conditions to develop. Fluid pahoehoe lava flows at temperatures exceeding one thousand degrees, [[b1]] rapidly along its upper crust when exposed to air. Because basalt has low thermal [[b2]], the interior remains liquid and continues moving downslope, leaving an empty [[b3]] once eruption stops.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "cooling"}, {"id": "B", "text": "conductivity"}, {"id": "C", "text": "chamber"}, {"id": "D", "text": "solidification"}, {"id": "E", "text": "insulation"}, {"id": "F", "text": "cavern"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["cooling", "conductivity", "chamber", "solidification", "insulation", "cavern"], "correctAnswer": "cooling"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["cooling", "conductivity", "chamber", "solidification", "insulation", "cavern"], "correctAnswer": "conductivity"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["cooling", "conductivity", "chamber", "solidification", "insulation", "cavern"], "correctAnswer": "chamber"}]'::jsonb,
     'Lava is cooling on its crust (chilling), low thermal conductivity prevents heat escape (insulation), leaving an empty chamber (tunnel).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rfib', 1, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-05-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Volcanic Speleothems: Mineral Drips', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The interior surfaces of evacuated volcanic conduits exhibit unusual mineral formations. Hot volcanic gases remelt ceiling rock, causing liquid basalt to drip and form slender [[b1]]. Unlike carbonate stalactites, these structures form in a single eruptive [[b2]] and cannot regenerate if broken by visiting [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "lavacicles"}, {"id": "B", "text": "episode"}, {"id": "C", "text": "spelunkers"}, {"id": "D", "text": "stalactites"}, {"id": "E", "text": "eruption"}, {"id": "F", "text": "explorers"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["lavacicles", "episode", "spelunkers", "stalactites", "eruption", "explorers"], "correctAnswer": "lavacicles"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["lavacicles", "episode", "spelunkers", "stalactites", "eruption", "explorers"], "correctAnswer": "episode"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["lavacicles", "episode", "spelunkers", "stalactites", "eruption", "explorers"], "correctAnswer": "spelunkers"}]'::jsonb,
     'Drips form lavacicles (lava stalactites), during a single eruptive episode (event), destroyed by spelunkers (cave visitors).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rfib', 2, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-05-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Subterranean Ecology: Sensory Evolution', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Animals dwelling in complete subterranean darkness face unique survival pressures. To detect prey without eyesight, cave-adapted invertebrates develop specialized [[b1]] hairs and extended antennae. In addition, their reduced metabolic [[b2]] allows them to survive long intervals between sporadic food [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "tactile"}, {"id": "B", "text": "demand"}, {"id": "C", "text": "supplies"}, {"id": "D", "text": "chemical"}, {"id": "E", "text": "consumption"}, {"id": "F", "text": "resources"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["tactile", "demand", "supplies", "chemical", "consumption", "resources"], "correctAnswer": "tactile"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["tactile", "demand", "supplies", "chemical", "consumption", "resources"], "correctAnswer": "demand"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["tactile", "demand", "supplies", "chemical", "consumption", "resources"], "correctAnswer": "supplies"}]'::jsonb,
     'Invertebrates develop tactile hairs (touch receptors), reduced metabolic demand (energy needs), during scarce supplies (food availability).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-005', 'g-pr89-005-rfib', 3, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-05-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Chemolithotrophic Life: Mineral Biofilms', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
