    ('q-pr89-single-06-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer',
     'Aerodynamic Mechanisms: Leading-Edge Vortex', 'In paragraph D, what is the primary role of the leading-edge vortex (LEV) during an insect''s wing downstroke?',
     NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "It creates a pocket of intense low pressure above the wing that generates powerful upward suction lift"}, {"id": "B", "text": "It warms the surrounding air to prevent ice accumulation on delicate wing membranes"}, {"id": "C", "text": "It deflects sound waves to prevent nocturnal predators from hearing the flapping sound"}, {"id": "D", "text": "It forces air backward to act as a miniature jet propulsion exhaust"}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
     'Paragraph D states that the leading-edge vortex generates a localized pocket of intense low atmospheric pressure above the wing, producing an upward suction force that generates substantial lift.', 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-006', 'g-pr89-006-single', 4, TRUE, 90, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-single-06-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'reading-mcq-single', 'Multiple Choice, Single Answer',
     'Biomimetic Robotics: Drone Miniaturization', 'According to paragraph F, why are flapping wings preferred over rotary propellers for millimeter-scale micro air vehicles?',
     NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Rotary motors cannot operate when exposed to ordinary atmospheric oxygen"}, {"id": "B", "text": "Flapping wings are immune to damage from electrical power surges"}, {"id": "C", "text": "International aviation regulations prohibit propeller-driven drones below one centimetre"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Miniature propellers suffer severe efficiency losses in viscous, low-Reynolds-number airflows"}]'::jsonb, '["D"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
