    ('q-pr89-rwfib-07-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Tyrian Purple: Luxury Status', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'In the ancient world, no dyed fabric held more political significance than Tyrian purple. Reserved for royalty and high magistrates, the crimson-violet pigment was [[b1]] with imperial sovereignty. Its price routinely exceeded its weight in gold, reflecting the intense labour required to [[b2]] thousands of marine snails. Consequently, the Roman senate enacted sumptuary laws to [[b3]] the wearing of solid purple robes to the reigning emperor.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["associated", "confused", "contrasted", "incompatible"], "correctAnswer": "associated"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["discard", "harvest", "scatter", "squander"], "correctAnswer": "harvest"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["allot", "disseminate", "extend", "restrict"], "correctAnswer": "restrict"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''associated with'' is the standard collocation for connection (''contrasted with'' means opposite; ''confused with'' means mistaken; ''incompatible with'' means conflicting). b2: ''harvest'' describes gathering snails (''squander'', ''discard'', and ''disperse'' mean wasting or scattering). b3: ''restrict ... to'' is the correct sumptuary construction (''allot'', ''disseminate'', and ''extend'' mean broadening access).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-07-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Murex Secretions: Biochemical Precursors', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Living marine snails do not directly contain finished purple pigment within their anatomy. Instead, their hypobranchial glands synthesize clear mucosal fluids containing chemical [[b1]] and specialized enzymes. In natural conditions, these secretions serve as an antimicrobial [[b2]] defending snail eggs from biological infection. When dyers crush the glands, enzymatic reactions yield unstable molecules that initiate the [[b3]] of the dye.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["byproducts", "contaminants", "precursors", "residues"], "correctAnswer": "precursors"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["barrier", "conduit", "gateway", "passage"], "correctAnswer": "barrier"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["decay", "dissolution", "evaporation", "formation"], "correctAnswer": "formation"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''precursors'' denotes colorless chemical starting materials (''byproducts'', ''residues'', and ''contaminants'' denote waste). b2: ''barrier'' describes cellular separation preventing premature reaction (''conduit'', ''passage'', and ''gateway'' mean open channels). b3: ''formation'' describes synthesizing dye (''dissolution'', ''decay'', and ''evaporation'' mean breaking down).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-07-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Photochemical Cascade: Color Transformation', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The development of Tyrian purple relies on an extraordinary photochemical reaction. When clear snail secretions are exposed to sunlight, they undergo rapid [[b1]] dimerization. The applied fluid visibly changes from yellow through turquoise before [[b2]] into an insoluble purple pigment. The primary chemical compound responsible for this intense coloration is [[b3]] as 6,6''-dibromoindigo.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["dormant", "inert", "oxidative", "quiescent"], "correctAnswer": "oxidative"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["dissolving", "evaporating", "liquefying", "precipitating"], "correctAnswer": "precipitating"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["concealed", "disregarded", "fabricated", "identified"], "correctAnswer": "identified"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''oxidative'' describes air/light chemical transformation (''inert'', ''quiescent'', and ''dormant'' mean unreactive). b2: ''precipitating'' means insoluble dye falling out of solution (''dissolving'', ''evaporating'', and ''liquefying'' mean turning to liquid/vapor). b3: ''identified'' describes scientific characterization (''concealed'' means hidden; ''fabricated'' means forged; ''disregarded'' means ignored).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-07-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Vat Fermentation: Alkaline Reduction', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Because pure purple pigment cannot dissolve in water, dyeing fabric required a chemical reduction process. Artisans simmered crushed snails in an alkaline bath containing stale urine to create an oxygen-depleted [[b1]]. In this vat, the purple compound was reduced to its soluble yellow base, which readily [[b2]] into raw wool fibers. Once lifted into the open air, oxygen permanently [[b3]] the color inside the fabric.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["crystal", "environment", "solid", "vacuum"], "correctAnswer": "environment"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["absorbed", "expelled", "repelled", "shed"], "correctAnswer": "absorbed"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["dislodged", "locked", "loosened", "released"], "correctAnswer": "locked"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''environment'' (reducing chemical environment) describes vat conditions (''vacuum'', ''solid'', and ''crystal'' are contextually impossible). b2: ''absorbed'' describes soluble dye penetrating wool fibers (''repelled'', ''shed'', and ''expelled'' mean rejected). b3: ''locked'' describes insoluble dye trapped inside fibers upon oxidation (''loosened'', ''released'', and ''dislodged'' mean escaping).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-07-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Byzantine Monopoly: Imperial Restriction', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'In the later centuries of the Roman and Byzantine empires, purple production was placed under state control. The imperial administration established a legal [[b1]] centered at the capital of Constantinople. Unauthorized manufacturing or commercial possession of imperial silks was classified as [[b2]], carrying severe penalties. This centralized control eventually [[b3]] when the empire collapsed following the Fourth Crusade.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["monopoly", "subsidy", "tariff", "tribute"], "correctAnswer": "monopoly"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["charity", "pardon", "treason", "tribute"], "correctAnswer": "treason"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["prospered", "solidified", "triumphed", "unraveled"], "correctAnswer": "unraveled"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''monopoly'' describes exclusive state control (''subsidy'', ''tribute'', and ''tariff'' denote financial mechanisms, not production control). b2: ''treason'' (laesa maiestas) is capital crime against the emperor (''pardon'' and ''charity'' are acts of mercy; ''tribute'' is payment). b3: ''unraveled'' describes industry collapse (''prospered'', ''solidified'', and ''triumphed'' mean succeeding).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-07-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Ancient Dye Harvesting: Murex Sourcing', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The manufacture of royal purple was an extractive industry on a colossal scale. Ancient dyers caught thousands of predatory sea [[b1]] in baited wicker traps set along coastal rocky shoals. Once brought ashore, workers carefully crushed the shell whorl to extract the minute hypobranchial [[b2]], leaving behind immense middens of discarded [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "snails"}, {"id": "B", "text": "gland"}, {"id": "C", "text": "shells"}, {"id": "D", "text": "molluscs"}, {"id": "E", "text": "tissue"}, {"id": "F", "text": "crusts"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["snails", "gland", "shells", "molluscs", "tissue", "crusts"], "correctAnswer": "snails"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["snails", "gland", "shells", "molluscs", "tissue", "crusts"], "correctAnswer": "gland"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["snails", "gland", "shells", "molluscs", "tissue", "crusts"], "correctAnswer": "shells"}]'::jsonb,
     'Dyers caught predatory sea snails (molluscs), extracted the hypobranchial gland (organ), leaving middens of shells (remains).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rfib', 1, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-07-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Color Variations: Murex Blending', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Phoenician artisans mastered the art of calibrating distinct shades of purple textiles. By blending secretions from different snail [[b1]], they altered the chemical proportions of red indirubin and blue indigo. This skilled formulation produced a spectrum of luxurious [[b2]] ranging from bright reddish-scarlet to deep imperial [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "species"}, {"id": "B", "text": "hues"}, {"id": "C", "text": "violet"}, {"id": "D", "text": "varieties"}, {"id": "E", "text": "shades"}, {"id": "F", "text": "crimson"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["species", "hues", "violet", "varieties", "shades", "crimson"], "correctAnswer": "species"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["species", "hues", "violet", "varieties", "shades", "crimson"], "correctAnswer": "hues"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["species", "hues", "violet", "varieties", "shades", "crimson"], "correctAnswer": "violet"}]'::jsonb,
     'Dyers blended secretions from different species (snail varieties), producing luxurious hues (colors), ranging to imperial violet (purple).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-007', 'g-pr89-007-rfib', 2, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-07-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Industrial Dye Works: Malodorous Zoning', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Operating ancient dye facilities presented serious environmental and municipal challenges. The prolonged simmering of rotting mollusc flesh in alkaline solutions generated a pervasive and sickening [[b1]]. Consequently, municipal authorities required dye factories to be established downwind, far beyond urban [[b2]], where prevailing sea breezes dispersed the offensive [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "stench"}, {"id": "B", "text": "boundaries"}, {"id": "C", "text": "vapors"}, {"id": "D", "text": "odor"}, {"id": "E", "text": "perimeters"}, {"id": "F", "text": "fumes"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["stench", "boundaries", "vapors", "odor", "perimeters", "fumes"], "correctAnswer": "stench"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["stench", "boundaries", "vapors", "odor", "perimeters", "fumes"], "correctAnswer": "boundaries"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["stench", "boundaries", "vapors", "odor", "perimeters", "fumes"], "correctAnswer": "vapors"}]'::jsonb,
     'Simmering flesh produced a sickening stench (odor), situated beyond urban boundaries (city limits), dispersing offensive vapors (fumes).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
