    ('q-pr89-rwfib-08-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Amber Fossilization: Soft Tissue Defense', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'While most fossils consist of mineralized bones and shells, amber preserves soft-bodied organisms with exceptional fidelity. Originating as an exudate produced by ancient trees, resin acted as an active defense to [[b1]] bark beetles and fungal infections. Small insects that came into contact with fresh resin blebs were completely enveloped. This sticky fluid sealed specimens from atmospheric oxygen, [[b2]] their delicate tissues from rapid microbial [[b3]].', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["deter", "harbour", "invite", "nurture"], "correctAnswer": "deter"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["aerating", "exposing", "insulating", "venting"], "correctAnswer": "insulating"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["decay", "germination", "growth", "proliferation"], "correctAnswer": "decay"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''deter'' describes terpene chemicals repelling pests (''invite'', ''nurture'', and ''harbour'' mean attracting or sheltering). b2: ''insulating'' describes sealing inclusions from air (''exposing'', ''venting'', and ''aerating'' mean opening to oxygen). b3: ''decay'' denotes microbial decomposition (''growth'', ''proliferation'', and ''germination'' mean flourishing).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-008', 'g-pr89-008-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-08-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Resin Polymerization: Copal Maturation', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'The transformation of tree resin into durable amber is a multi-stage geochemical process. Resin differs fundamentally from sap, which is a watery fluid that [[b1]] nutrients throughout the plant. When exposed to air, volatile solvents in resin evaporate, leaving a tacky solid. Over millions of years, heat and pressure cause molecules to [[b2]], turning the substance first into copal and then into true amber, which [[b3]] chemical weathering.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["confines", "impedes", "stagnates", "transports"], "correctAnswer": "transports"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["dissolve", "evaporate", "liquefy", "polymerize"], "correctAnswer": "polymerize"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["resists", "succumbs", "surrenders", "yields"], "correctAnswer": "resists"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''transports'' describes water carrying resin to sediments (''impedes'', ''stagnates'', and ''confines'' mean stopping flow). b2: ''polymerize'' is the exact chemical cross-linking process (''evaporate'', ''dissolve'', and ''liquefy'' mean breaking or vaporizing). b3: ''resists'' describes amber enduring solvents (''succumbs to'', ''yields to'', and ''surrenders to'' mean being destroyed).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-008', 'g-pr89-008-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-08-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Amber Inclusions: Behavioral Snapshots', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Because resin entraps creatures almost instantaneously, inclusions capture fleeting moments of prehistoric life. Paleontologists have discovered amber pieces that [[b1]] spiders wrapping prey in silk or ants locked in combat. Delicate structures like spider webs and fungal spores remain perfectly intact. However, amber exhibits a distinct taphonomic [[b2]], as tree-dwelling creatures are vastly [[b3]] compared to bottom-dwelling marine organisms.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["distort", "eradicate", "falsify", "preserve"], "correctAnswer": "preserve"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["balance", "bias", "clarity", "neutrality"], "correctAnswer": "bias"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["diminished", "excluded", "overlooked", "overrepresented"], "correctAnswer": "overrepresented"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''preserve'' describes capturing behavioral moments (''eradicate'' means destroy; ''distort'' and ''falsify'' mean corrupting). b2: ''bias'' denotes systematic sampling skew (''clarity'', ''balance'', and ''neutrality'' mean lack of skew). b3: ''overrepresented'' matches arboreal insects being caught much more than ground species (''excluded'', ''diminished'', and ''overlooked'' mean underrepresented).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-008', 'g-pr89-008-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-08-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Digital Synchrotrons: Non-Destructive Imaging', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Modern imaging techniques have fundamentally transformed how researchers study amber fossils. In the past, scientists were forced to manually polish nodules, which [[b1]] shattering fragile specimens. Today, high-resolution synchrotron computed tomography allows researchers to [[b2]] specimens digitally. This non-invasive technology creates detailed three-dimensional models of internal organs without [[b3]] the physical stone.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["averted", "precluded", "prevented", "risked"], "correctAnswer": "risked"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["assemble", "coalesce", "dissect", "unify"], "correctAnswer": "dissect"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["damaging", "enhancing", "restoring", "securing"], "correctAnswer": "damaging"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''risked'' describes physical slicing endangering specimens (''prevented'', ''precluded'', and ''averted'' mean avoiding danger). b2: ''dissect'' means cutting open (''unify'', ''coalesce'', and ''assemble'' mean putting together). b3: ''damaging'' describes harming fragile fossils (''restoring'', ''enhancing'', and ''securing'' mean improving safety).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-008', 'g-pr89-008-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-08-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Ancient DNA Limits: Hydrolysis Reality', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Early speculations that amber could preserve intact prehistoric DNA have been refuted by biochemical research. Rigorous experiments demonstrate that nucleic acids undergo spontaneous [[b1]] even within dry, airtight resin. Within fossils that are millions of years old, genetic bonds have completely [[b2]]. Although amber cannot resurrect extinct creatures, it provides an invaluable window into ancient ecological [[b3]].', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["fermentation", "hydrolysis", "photosynthesis", "respiration"], "correctAnswer": "hydrolysis"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["amplified", "degraded", "fortified", "synthesized"], "correctAnswer": "degraded"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["chasms", "interactions", "omissions", "voids"], "correctAnswer": "interactions"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''hydrolysis'' is the chemical bond cleavage by water (''photosynthesis'', ''fermentation'', and ''respiration'' are living metabolic processes). b2: ''degraded'' describes ancient DNA breaking into tiny fragments (''fortified'', ''synthesized'', and ''amplified'' mean making stronger or more abundant). b3: ''interactions'' denotes ecological host-parasite relationships (''voids'', ''chasms'', and ''omissions'' denote physical gaps).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-008', 'g-pr89-008-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
