     'Resin Chemistry: Molecular Differences', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Botanical resin serves an important defensive role in woodland ecosystems. Unlike nutrient-bearing plant sap, resin is composed of sticky [[b1]] and non-volatile acids. When bark is wounded, the resin flows over the breach and hardens, creating a durable [[b2]] that prevents parasitic insects from establishing a [[b3]] inside the wood.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "terpenes"}, {"id": "B", "text": "seal"}, {"id": "C", "text": "colony"}, {"id": "D", "text": "resins"}, {"id": "E", "text": "barrier"}, {"id": "F", "text": "swarm"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["terpenes", "seal", "colony", "resins", "barrier", "swarm"], "correctAnswer": "terpenes"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["terpenes", "seal", "colony", "resins", "barrier", "swarm"], "correctAnswer": "seal"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["terpenes", "seal", "colony", "resins", "barrier", "swarm"], "correctAnswer": "colony"}]'::jsonb,
