     'Cretaceous amber from northern Myanmar provides unprecedented views into the dinosaur era. Researchers have uncovered juvenile bird [[b1]] with intact feathers, along with ancient ticks grasping dinosaur down. These exceptional inclusions offer direct fossil [[b2]] of complex host-parasite [[b3]] that existed nearly one hundred million years ago.', '[{"id": "A", "text": "wings"}, {"id": "B", "text": "proof"}, {"id": "C", "text": "dynamics"}, {"id": "D", "text": "plumage"}, {"id": "E", "text": "evidence"}, {"id": "F", "text": "behavior"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["wings", "proof", "dynamics", "plumage", "evidence", "behavior"], "correctAnswer": "wings"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["wings", "proof", "dynamics", "plumage", "evidence", "behavior"], "correctAnswer": "proof"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["wings", "proof", "dynamics", "plumage", "evidence", "behavior"], "correctAnswer": "dynamics"}]'::jsonb,
