     'Ecological Sampling: Arboreal Habitat Bias', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Fossil assemblages preserved in amber do not represent an unbiased picture of prehistoric ecosystems. Because resin forms upon the exterior trunks of ancient [[b1]], it primarily traps creatures that crawl across bark. Consequently, ground-dwelling species and open-water organisms are almost entirely [[b2]] from the fossil [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "trees"}, {"id": "B", "text": "absent"}, {"id": "C", "text": "record"}, {"id": "D", "text": "canopies"}, {"id": "E", "text": "scarce"}, {"id": "F", "text": "archive"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["trees", "absent", "record", "canopies", "scarce", "archive"], "correctAnswer": "trees"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["trees", "absent", "record", "canopies", "scarce", "archive"], "correctAnswer": "absent"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["trees", "absent", "record", "canopies", "scarce", "archive"], "correctAnswer": "record"}]'::jsonb,
     'Resin forms on trees (woody trunks), leaving ground species absent (missing), from the fossil record (paleontological archive).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
