    ('q-pr89-rfib-08-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Molecular Decay: DNA Fragmentation', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Biochemical investigations have established that genetic material cannot endure indefinitely. Exposure to trace moisture inside resin triggers spontaneous [[b1]] that cleaves DNA chains into tiny pieces. Over geological time, this chemical disintegration leaves no functional [[b2]] that could ever be used for cloning extinct [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "reactions"}, {"id": "B", "text": "sequences"}, {"id": "C", "text": "animals"}, {"id": "D", "text": "processes"}, {"id": "E", "text": "fragments"}, {"id": "F", "text": "organisms"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["reactions", "sequences", "animals", "processes", "fragments", "organisms"], "correctAnswer": "reactions"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["reactions", "sequences", "animals", "processes", "fragments", "organisms"], "correctAnswer": "sequences"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["reactions", "sequences", "animals", "processes", "fragments", "organisms"], "correctAnswer": "animals"}]'::jsonb,
