     'Resin Maturation: Chemical Polymerization', 'How does tree resin differ from tree sap (paragraph B)?',
     NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Sap is a watery nutrient-carrying fluid, whereas resin is a complex mixture of non-volatile terpenoids and acids"}, {"id": "B", "text": "Sap hardens into amber, whereas resin dissolves completely in rainwater"}, {"id": "C", "text": "Resin is produced exclusively by marine algae, while sap is produced by conifers"}, {"id": "D", "text": "Sap is highly toxic and causes spontaneous cross-linking of wood fibers"}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
