    ('q-pr89-rwfib-10-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Granular Physics: Classical State Defiance', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Despite its ubiquity, granular material defies simple classification. When resting in a stationary heap, dry sand maintains its shape like a solid and can [[b1]] compressive loads. When poured through a container opening, it flows continuously and [[b2]] to the shape of the vessel like a fluid. Finally, when shaken vigorously, individual grains bounce chaotically and disperse like a gas. Because interactions are dominated by friction rather than thermal motion, granular matter operates under [[b3]] physical laws.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["dodge", "evade", "forfeit", "support"], "correctAnswer": "support"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["conforms", "dissents", "objects", "rebels"], "correctAnswer": "conforms"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["conventional", "distinct", "identical", "standard"], "correctAnswer": "distinct"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''support'' describes bearing compressive loads (''evade'', ''dodge'', and ''forfeit'' describe avoiding actions). b2: ''conforms to'' is the correct prepositional construction for taking the shape of a vessel (''dissents from'', ''rebels against'', and ''objects to'' take different prepositions and meanings). b3: ''distinct'' describes unique non-classical laws (''identical'', ''conventional'', and ''standard'' mean ordinary or identical).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rwfib', 1, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-10-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Force Chains: Stress Networks', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Unlike solid metals where mechanical stress distributes evenly, granular packs transmit force through filamentary networks. Specialized lines of touching grains, known as force chains, bear the vast [[b1]] of the applied weight while adjacent particles remain largely unstressed. Because these chains are directional, a minor shift in external pressure can cause them to [[b2]] suddenly. When force chains fail, a stable heap can instantaneously [[b3]] into a moving avalanche.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["fraction", "majority", "minority", "scarcity"], "correctAnswer": "majority"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["buckle", "solidify", "stiffen", "strengthen"], "correctAnswer": "buckle"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["fossilize", "freeze", "liquefy", "petrify"], "correctAnswer": "liquefy"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''majority of'' denotes bearing the bulk of weight (''minority'', ''scarcity'', and ''fraction'' mean very little). b2: ''buckle'' describes force chains collapsing under pressure (''strengthen'', ''solidify'', and ''stiffen'' mean resisting collapse). b3: ''liquefy'' describes sand transitioning into a flowing fluid avalanche (''freeze'', ''petrify'', and ''fossilize'' mean turning into solid rock).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rwfib', 2, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-10-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Angle of Repose: Self-Organized Criticality', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'When dry sand is poured onto a surface, it forms a conical heap that approaches a maximum slope called the angle of repose. At this critical threshold, the pile exhibits self-organized criticality, where internal stability is delicately [[b1]]. Adding a single extra grain to the summit can [[b2]] anything from a tiny shift to a massive landslide. The frequency of these avalanches follows a power-law distribution, showing that catastrophic events can occur without [[b3]] triggers.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["balanced", "skewed", "toppled", "warped"], "correctAnswer": "balanced"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["avert", "prevent", "stifle", "trigger"], "correctAnswer": "trigger"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["endogenous", "external", "internal", "intrinsic"], "correctAnswer": "external"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''balanced'' describes critical threshold equilibrium (''skewed'', ''warped'', and ''toppled'' mean uncoordinated or fallen). b2: ''trigger'' describes a grain causing an avalanche (''prevent'', ''stifle'', and ''avert'' mean stopping). b3: ''external'' triggers explains that internal dynamics alone cause avalanches (''internal'', ''intrinsic'', and ''endogenous'' mean internal forces).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rwfib', 3, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-10-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Brazil Nut Effect: Size Segregation', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'Shaking a mixture of different-sized particles produces unexpected sorting. When a container of mixed grains is vibrated vertically, larger and denser particles frequently [[b1]] to the surface while smaller grains sink. This occurs partly because small particles easily [[b2]] through temporary gaps beneath large objects. In addition, convective currents carry large particles upward, leaving them [[b3]] on top.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["descend", "rise", "sink", "subside"], "correctAnswer": "rise"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["climb", "rebound", "soar", "trickle"], "correctAnswer": "trickle"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["buried", "drowned", "stranded", "submerged"], "correctAnswer": "stranded"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''rise'' describes large particles moving upward (''sink'', ''subside'', and ''descend'' mean moving down). b2: ''trickle through'' describes small grains falling through voids (''rebound'', ''soar'', and ''climb'' mean moving up or bouncing). b3: ''stranded on top'' describes large grains trapped on the surface (''submerged'', ''buried'', and ''drowned'' mean underneath).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rwfib', 4, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rwfib-10-05', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Fill in the Blanks (Dropdown)',
     'Hopper Jamming: Industrial Arches', 'Below is a text with blanks. Click on each blank, a list of choices will appear. Select the appropriate answer choice for each blank.',
     'In industrial manufacturing, controlling granular discharge is essential for processing powders and grain. As particles funnel toward a discharge opening, they frequently form interlocking arches that [[b1]] flow. When these stress bridges collapse unpredictably, the sudden rush of falling mass can [[b2]] storage silos. Engineers install acoustic vibrators and flow inserts to systematically [[b3]] these obstructive arches.', '[]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["accelerate", "facilitate", "halt", "smooth"], "correctAnswer": "halt"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["fortify", "reinforce", "rupture", "secure"], "correctAnswer": "rupture"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["disrupt", "nurture", "preserve", "sustain"], "correctAnswer": "disrupt"}]'::jsonb,
     'b1: ''halt'' describes arches blocking flow (''facilitate'', ''accelerate'', and ''smooth'' mean assisting flow). b2: ''rupture'' describes sudden falling mass bursting silos (''reinforce'', ''secure'', and ''fortify'' mean making stronger). b3: ''disrupt'' describes acoustic vibrators breaking arches (''nurture'', ''preserve'', and ''sustain'' mean maintaining arches).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rwfib', 5, TRUE, 150, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-10-01', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Granular Dynamics: Dissipative Collisions', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Understanding granular movement requires analyzing friction between particles. Unlike gas molecules that collide elastically without loss of momentum, colliding grains lose kinetic [[b1]] through frictional contact. This constant energy dissipation means that a granular system will rapidly come to a [[b2]] unless an external source supplies ongoing [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "energy"}, {"id": "B", "text": "rest"}, {"id": "C", "text": "vibration"}, {"id": "D", "text": "motion"}, {"id": "E", "text": "equilibrium"}, {"id": "F", "text": "agitation"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["energy", "rest", "vibration", "motion", "equilibrium", "agitation"], "correctAnswer": "energy"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["energy", "rest", "vibration", "motion", "equilibrium", "agitation"], "correctAnswer": "rest"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["energy", "rest", "vibration", "motion", "equilibrium", "agitation"], "correctAnswer": "vibration"}]'::jsonb,
     'Grains lose kinetic energy (heat loss), coming to a complete rest (stopping), unless supplied with vibration (agitation).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rfib', 1, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-10-02', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Stress Transmission: Unjamming Transitions', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'The internal stability of a sand heap depends on microscopic contact points. Fragile force chains support the weight of the pile by transferring stress along linear [[b1]]. If an external disturbance shifts the orientation of key grains, these chains can buckle, causing the solid structure to [[b2]] into a fluid-like [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "pathways"}, {"id": "B", "text": "collapse"}, {"id": "C", "text": "flow"}, {"id": "D", "text": "chains"}, {"id": "E", "text": "disruption"}, {"id": "F", "text": "discharge"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["pathways", "collapse", "flow", "chains", "disruption", "discharge"], "correctAnswer": "pathways"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["pathways", "collapse", "flow", "chains", "disruption", "discharge"], "correctAnswer": "collapse"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["pathways", "collapse", "flow", "chains", "disruption", "discharge"], "correctAnswer": "flow"}]'::jsonb,
     'Stress transfers along linear pathways (force chains), causing the structure to collapse (fail), into a fluid-like flow (avalanche).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rfib', 2, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-10-03', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Silo Engineering: Asymmetric Ruptures', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
     'Storing bulk agricultural grain inside tall concrete structures involves serious mechanical risks. When grain funnels unevenly toward an exit hatch, it generates asymmetrical lateral [[b1]] against the interior walls. These sudden stress differentials can buckle structural steel and cause catastrophic silo [[b2]], threatening human safety and industrial [[b3]].', '[{"id": "A", "text": "pressures"}, {"id": "B", "text": "failures"}, {"id": "C", "text": "operations"}, {"id": "D", "text": "stresses"}, {"id": "E", "text": "fractures"}, {"id": "F", "text": "processes"}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["pressures", "failures", "operations", "stresses", "fractures", "processes"], "correctAnswer": "pressures"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["pressures", "failures", "operations", "stresses", "fractures", "processes"], "correctAnswer": "failures"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["pressures", "failures", "operations", "stresses", "fractures", "processes"], "correctAnswer": "operations"}]'::jsonb,
     'Grain exerts lateral pressures (forces on walls), causing structural failures (collapses), disrupting operations (business activity).', 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE Reading', 'Original practice', 'Batch D'],
     'rp-pr89-010', 'g-pr89-010-rfib', 3, TRUE, 120, NULL),
    ('q-pr89-rfib-10-04', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks',
     'Percolation Mechanics: Void Infiltration', 'In the text below some words are missing. Drag words from the box below to the appropriate place in the text. To undo an answer choice, drag the word back to the box below the text.',
