     'Ancient Roman Mosaic Tesserae Crafting', 'The text boxes below have been placed in a random order. Restore the original order.',
     NULL, '[{"id": "p5", "text": "Finally, liquid grout was rubbed across the joints and the surface was polished with abrasive sand to create a seamless, durable pavement."}, {"id": "p3", "text": "On top of a leveled rubble foundation, workers spread a fresh bedding layer of wet lime and pozzolan mortar."}, {"id": "p2", "text": "Artisans created these intricate decorative surfaces by cutting colored stones, marble, and colored glass into tiny cubical pieces called tesserae."}, {"id": "p1", "text": "In ancient Roman architecture, decorative floor mosaics were an essential feature of public villas and bathhouses."}, {"id": "p4", "text": "Craftsmen pressed individual tesserae firmly into this damp mortar bed according to painted geometric patterns."}]'::jsonb, '["p1", "p2", "p3", "p4", "p5"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb,
